   "start": 58.07,
   "end": 70.44,
   "text": "And exhale, letting your shoulders drop a little as you do."
  },
  {
   "start": 70.29,
   "end": 73.96,
   "text": "One more time."
  },
  {
   "start": 73.81,
   "end": 79.18,
   "text": "Inhale\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 79.03,
   "end": 88.48,
   "text": "and exhale."
  },
  {
   "start": 88.33,
   "end": 95.3,
   "text": "I want you to think of a moment recently when you had to wait for something."
  },
  {
   "start": 95.15,
   "end": 99.56,
   "text": "Maybe a line somewhere."
  },
  {
   "start": 99.41,
   "end": 104.4,
   "text": "Maybe a message that hadn't come yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 104.25,
   "end": 109.48,
   "text": "Maybe just a moment where someone else was speaking,and you had to"
  },
  {
   "start": 109.33,
   "end": 114.38,
   "text": "wait for them to finish so that you could say something."
  },
  {
   "start": 114.23,
   "end": 125.24,
   "text": "Bring that feeling gently into your mind."
  },
  {
   "start": 125.09,
   "end": 133.46,
   "text": "Notice what happens in your body when waiting feels hard."
  },
  {
   "start": 133.31,
   "end": 137.64,
   "text": "Sometimes your leg starts moving."
  },
  {
   "start": 137.49,
   "end": 143.18,
   "text": "Maybe your breath gets a little shorter."
  },
  {
   "start": 143.03,
   "end": 149.16,
   "text": "Maybe your mind starts thinking about what will happen next instead of"
  },
  {
   "start": 149.01,
   "end": 155.06,
   "text": "focusing on the present"
  },
  {
   "start": 154.91,
   "end": 163.6,
   "text": "Inhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 163.45,
   "end": 173.04,
   "text": "This feeling of always wanting things to happen faster is called impatience."
  },
  {
   "start": 172.89,
   "end": 176.98,
   "text": "You want to move ahead instead of waiting."
  },
  {
   "start": 176.83,
   "end": 182.96,
   "text": "Often, it comes from feeling like it should already be your turn."
  },
  {
   "start": 182.81,
   "end": 192.14,
   "text": "\u201cYour turn\u201d simply means the moment when it\u2019s time for you to do something."
  },
  {
   "start": 191.99,
   "end": 199.22,
   "text": "Before your turn, other people or things may need to go first."
  },
  {
   "start": 199.07,
   "end": 210.28,
   "text": "Think of a line at a supermarket checkout counter: everyone waits until it's their turn."
  },
  {
   "start": 210.13,
   "end": 222.08,
   "text": "Exhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 221.93,
   "end": 224.78,
   "text": "Notice, honestly,"
  },
  {
   "start": 224.63,
   "end": 234.04,
   "text": "if there is a part of you right now that feels like it's been waiting a little too long for its turn."
  },
  {
   "start": 233.89,
   "end": 238.02,
   "text": "Maybe about something small today."
  },
  {
   "start": 237.87,
   "end": 244.7,
   "text": "Maybe about something much bigger in your life."
  },
  {
   "start": 244.55,
   "end": 251.96,
   "text": "Inhale again."
  },
  {
   "start": 251.81,
   "end": 258.14,
   "text": "Here's something worth noticing about lines like that."
  },
  {
   "start": 257.99,
   "end": 265.7,
   "text": "Everyone standing in them wants their turn just as much as you want yours."
  },
  {
   "start": 265.55,
   "end": 272.9,
   "text": "Nobody's turn actually skips ahead just because someone wants it badly enough."
  },
  {
   "start": 272.75,
   "end": 282.98,
   "text": "The line moves the way it moves, one person, one moment, at a time."
  },
  {
   "start": 282.83,
   "end": 293.32,
   "text": "Exhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 293.17,
   "end": 299.78,
   "text": "There is a skill in learning to wait your turn."
  },
  {
   "start": 299.63,
   "end": 308.62,
   "text": "It means letting things happen in the right order without rushing or forcing them."
  },
  {
   "start": 308.47,
   "end": 318.0,
   "text": "You trust that your moment will come, even when it\u2019s someone else\u2019s turn right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 317.85,
   "end": 323.98,
   "text": "Let's practice this, gently, right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 323.83,
   "end": 329.24,
   "text": "Inhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 329.09,
   "end": 334.46,
   "text": "Imagine you\u2019re standing in that same line."
  },
  {
   "start": 334.31,
   "end": 343.58,
   "text": "Instead of feeling restless or trying to move ahead, simply stand calmly where you are."
  },
  {
   "start": 343.43,
   "end": 346.58,
   "text": "Your turn has not disappeared."
  },
  {
   "start": 346.43,
   "end": 354.44,
   "text": "It just hasn't come yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 354.29,
   "end": 360.78,
   "text": "Exhale, and let your shoulders drop with that same realization:"
  },
  {
   "start": 360.63,
   "end": 370.56,
   "text": "not yet doesn't mean never."
  },
  {
   "start": 370.41,
   "end": 377.64,
   "text": "Not yet doesn't mean never."
  },
  {
   "start": 377.49,
   "end": 386.2,
   "text": "Notice your breath now, and let it move at its own natural rhythm,"
  },
  {
   "start": 386.05,
   "end": 392.08,
   "text": "without rushing it either."
  },
  {
   "start": 391.93,
   "end": 401.96,
   "text": "Even your breathing has its own turn, taking in air, and then, patiently, letting it go,"
  },
  {
   "start": 401.81,
   "end": 409.42,
   "text": "one at a time, never trying to inhale and exhale simultaneously,"
  },
  {
   "start": 409.27,
   "end": 415.2,
   "text": "never rushing that natural order."
  },
  {
   "start": 415.05,
   "end": 426.0,
   "text": "So now inhale again, noticing this rhythm."
  },
  {
   "start": 425.85,
   "end": 441.48,
   "text": "And exhale, noticing how naturally it happens, without force."
  },
  {
   "start": 441.33,
   "end": 447.28,
   "text": "This is what it means to wait your turn."
  },
  {
   "start": 447.13,
   "end": 460.26,
   "text": "You don't feel angry or tense."
  },
  {
   "start": 460.11,
   "end": 461.02,
   "text": "You simply slow down and trust that your time will come,"
  },
  {
   "start": 460.87,
   "end": 471.64,
   "text": "just like your breath comes naturally, not too early and not too late."
  },
  {
   "start": 471.49,
   "end": 477.42,
   "text": "Let 's inhale again."
  },
  {
   "start": 477.27,
   "end": 482.64,
   "text": "Bring to mind again whatever you're currently waiting for,"
  },
  {
   "start": 482.49,
   "end": 488.36,
   "text": "whatever moment still feels a little out of reach right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 488.21,
   "end": 499.3,
   "text": "Instead of pushing against it, try simply saying, quietly, \"My turn is coming.\""
  },
  {
   "start": 499.15,
   "end": 508.42,
   "text": "\"My turn is coming.\""
  },
  {
   "start": 508.27,
   "end": 515.78,
   "text": "Notice how that feels, even if it feels slightly unfamiliar."
  },
  {
   "start": 515.63,
   "end": 517.21,
   "text": "That's alright."
  },
  {
   "start": 517.06,
   "end": 529.29,
   "text": "Waiting patiently is a practice, not something that happens perfectly right away."
  },
  {
   "start": 529.14,
   "end": 543.08,
   "text": "Now let\u2019s exhale completely."
  },
  {
   "start": 542.93,
   "end": 547.64,
   "text": "You don't need to enjoy waiting."
  },
  {
   "start": 547.49,
   "end": 551.72,
   "text": "You just need to trust, a little more,"
  },
  {
   "start": 551.57,
   "end": 556.46,
   "text": "that waiting your turn doesn't mean being forgotten,"
  },
  {
   "start": 556.31,
   "end": 561.62,
   "text": "it simply means the line is moving the way it's supposed to,"
  },
  {
   "start": 561.47,
   "end": 571.4,
   "text": "and your moment is still somewhere ahead of you, closer now than it was a few minutes ago."
  },
  {
   "start": 571.25,
   "end": 578.06,
   "text": "You can wait your turn."
  },
  {
   "start": 577.91,
   "end": 585.16,
   "text": "And if you\u2019d like, you can repeat a few words after me."
  },
  {
   "start": 585.01,
   "end": 593.75,
   "text": "My turn is coming, even if it hasn't arrived yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 593.6,
   "end": 599.2,
   "text": "My turn is coming, even if it hasn't arrived yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 599.05,
   "end": 650.86,
   "text": "I don't have to push for something that's already on its way."
  },
  {
   "start": 650.71,
   "end": 659.18,
   "text": "I don't have to push for something that's already on its way."
  },
  {
   "start": 659.03,
   "end": 659.68,
   "text": "Waiting doesn't mean I've been forgotten."
  },
  {
   "start": 659.03,
   "end": 659.68,
   "text": "Waiting doesn't mean I've been forgotten."
  },
  {
   "start": 659.03,
   "end": 659.68,
   "text": "I trust the timing of my own life, even the waiting parts."
  },
  {
   "start": 659.03,
   "end": 659.68,
   "text": "I trust the timing of my own life, even the waiting parts."
  },
  {
   "start": 659.03,
   "end": 661.04,
   "text": "Take one more slow inhale."
  },
  {
   "start": 660.89,
   "end": 679.6,
   "text": "And exhale, completely."
  },
  {
   "start": 679.45,
   "end": 694.34,
   "text": "Feeling a little bit more patient, than when you begin."
  },
  {
   "start": 694.19,
   "end": 703.02,
   "text": "When you're ready to come back, start noticing small, real things around you."
  },
  {
   "start": 702.87,
   "end": 707.24,
   "text": "Whatever is supporting your body right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 707.09,
   "end": 710.46,
   "text": "Any sound nearby."
  },
  {
   "start": 710.31,
   "end": 719.16,
   "text": "Your breath."
  },
  {
   "start": 719.01,
   "end": 719.66,
   "text": "Your fingers."
  },
  {
   "start": 719.16,
   "end": 720.68,
   "text": "Then your feet."
  },
  {
   "start": 720.53,
   "end": 730.48,
   "text": "And whenever it feels right, let your eyes open."
  },
  {
   "start": 730.33,
   "end": 736.9,
   "text": "Carry this with you, into whatever waiting comes next in your day."
  },
  {
   "start": 736.75,
   "end": 742.32,
   "text": "Impatience may still visit sometimes, that's alright,"
  },
  {
   "start": 742.17,
   "end": 747.42,
   "text": "it's simply energy without anywhere to go yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 747.27,
   "end": 755.36,
   "text": "But you know, a little more clearly, how it feels to wait your turn, calmly,"
  },
  {
   "start": 755.21,
   "end": 765.0,
   "text": "and unhurried, trusting that your moment is still coming."
  }
 ]
}

assets/content/episodes/c004/cues.json:
{
 "source": "faster-whisper small.en word timestamps aligned to script phrases",
 "matchedWords": 795,
 "scriptWords": 812,
 "cues": [
  {
   "start": 0.95,
   "end": 4.82,
   "text": "Alright, let\u2019s take a little pause together."
  },
  {
   "start": 4.67,
   "end": 7.0,
   "text": "Okay?"
  },
  {
   "start": 6.85,
   "end": 11.74,
   "text": "Wherever you are, whatever your day has looked like so far,"
  },
  {
   "start": 11.59,
   "end": 16.53,
   "text": "you can leave it at the door for a few minutes."
  },
  {
   "start": 16.38,
   "end": 20.93,
   "text": "\u201cLeave it at the door\u201d is a metaphor that means giving yourself"
  },
  {
   "start": 20.78,
   "end": 26.59,
   "text": "permission to put everything else aside for a few minutes and focus"
  },
  {
   "start": 26.44,
   "end": 29.84,
   "text": "on being here."
  },
  {
   "start": 29.69,
   "end": 32.52,
   "text": "Get comfortable."
  },
  {
   "start": 32.37,
   "end": 38.77,
   "text": "Let yourself settle into the space you\u2019re in."
  },
  {
   "start": 38.62,
   "end": 43.16,
   "text": "You might close your eyes, if you want."
  },
  {
   "start": 43.01,
   "end": 46.99,
   "text": "There is nowhere you need to be right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.84,
   "end": 49.47,
   "text": "Nothing you need to do."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.32,
   "end": 51.91,
   "text": "Nothing you need to get right."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.76,
   "end": 55.11,
   "text": "Just a few moments to slow down and breathe."
  },
  {
   "start": 54.96,
   "end": 61.68,
   "text": "Take a gentle breath in\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 61.53,
   "end": 72.25,
   "text": "And let it go."
  },
  {
   "start": 72.1,
   "end": 78.45,
   "text": "Feel yourself settling a little more with each exhale."
  },
  {
   "start": 78.3,
   "end": 80.27,
   "text": "One more slow breath in\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 80.12,
   "end": 92.86,
   "text": "And out."
  },
  {
   "start": 92.71,
   "end": 96.13,
   "text": "I want you to notice something."
  },
  {
   "start": 95.98,
   "end": 100.99,
   "text": "Notice your mind, right now, exactly as it is."
  },
  {
   "start": 100.84,
   "end": 107.8,
   "text": "Not trying to change it, just noticing it."
  },
  {
   "start": 107.65,
   "end": 111.52,
   "text": "Maybe your mind is still a little busy."
  },
  {
   "start": 111.37,
   "end": 116.1,
   "text": "Maybe you replay in a conversation from earlier."
  },
  {
   "start": 115.95,
   "end": 122.39,
   "text": "Maybe going over something that hasn't ever, hasn't even happened yet."
  },
  {
   "start": 122.24,
   "end": 131.76,
   "text": "Maybe just circling the same thought, again and again, without really going anywhere new."
  },
  {
   "start": 131.61,
   "end": 134.38,
   "text": "That is called overthinking."
  },
  {
   "start": 134.23,
   "end": 145.82,
   "text": "To overthink means your mind keeps returning to the same worry, turning it over and over,"
  },
  {
   "start": 145.67,
   "end": 151.91,
   "text": "like a stone in your pocket you keep touching without meaning to,"
  },
  {
   "start": 151.76,
   "end": 158.22,
   "text": "without it actually getting smoother or smaller."
  },
  {
   "start": 158.07,
   "end": 164.31,
   "text": "Notice, gently, if there is a stone like that in your own mind right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 164.16,
   "end": 166.45,
   "text": "No need to push it away."
  },
  {
   "start": 166.3,
   "end": 172.0,
   "text": "Just notice it's there."
  },
  {
   "start": 171.85,
   "end": 178.5,
   "text": "Inhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 178.35,
   "end": 182.74,
   "text": "Here's something true about overthinking."
  },
  {
   "start": 182.59,
   "end": 190.39,
   "text": "It almost always lives in two places: the past or the future."
  },
  {
   "start": 190.24,
   "end": 197.95,
   "text": "It replaced what already happened, wondering if it could have gone differently."
  },
  {
   "start": 197.8,
   "end": 207.43,
   "text": "Or it imagines what hasn't happened yet, imagining every way it might go wrong."
  },
  {
   "start": 207.28,
   "end": 218.0,
   "text": "Notice, if you can, which one your mind tends to visit more: the past or the future."
  },
  {
   "start": 217.85,
   "end": 228.53,
   "text": "Exhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 228.38,
   "end": 233.59,
   "text": "Now, I want to bring you somewhere else entirely."
  },
  {
   "start": 233.44,
   "end": 236.01,
   "text": "Right here."
  },
  {
   "start": 235.86,
   "end": 240.98,
   "text": "Feel your body, exactly where it is, right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 240.83,
   "end": 244.24,
   "text": "Not where it was an hour ago."
  },
  {
   "start": 244.09,
   "end": 247.24,
   "text": "Not where it will be later today."
  },
  {
   "start": 247.09,
   "end": 258.39,
   "text": "Just here, in this exact chair, or this exact bed, this exact floor."
  },
  {
   "start": 258.24,
   "end": 263.48,
   "text": "This is what it means to be present."
  },
  {
   "start": 263.33,
   "end": 269.94,
   "text": "Being present simply means paying attention to what\u2019s happening right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 269.79,
   "end": 273.02,
   "text": "Not thinking about what happened before."
  },
  {
   "start": 272.87,
   "end": 276.8,
   "text": "Not worrying about what might happen later."
  },
  {
   "start": 276.65,
   "end": 283.42,
   "text": "Just being here, in this moment, and noticing what you can see, hear, feel,"
  },
  {
   "start": 283.27,
   "end": 286.39,
   "text": "and experience right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 286.24,
   "end": 289.46,
   "text": "Okay?"
  },
  {
   "start": 289.31,
   "end": 294.41,
   "text": "Inhale, and as you do, notice this breath."
  },
  {
   "start": 294.26,
   "end": 297.57,
   "text": "Not yesterday's breath."
  },
  {
   "start": 297.42,
   "end": 299.35,
   "text": "Not tomorrow's."
  },
  {
   "start": 299.2,
   "end": 311.05,
   "text": "This one, right now, entering your body."
  },
  {
   "start": 310.9,
   "end": 320.6,
   "text": "Exhale, and notice it leaving."
  },
  {
   "start": 320.45,
   "end": 322.74,
   "text": "Breath is strange."
  },
  {
   "start": 322.59,
   "end": 326.14,
   "text": "You can't breathe yesterday's air."
  },
  {
   "start": 325.99,
   "end": 330.02,
   "text": "You can't breathe tomorrow's either."
  },
  {
   "start": 329.87,
   "end": 337.73,
   "text": "Every single breath only ever happens in the present moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 337.58,
   "end": 345.32,
   "text": "Inhale again, slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 345.17,
   "end": 351.68,
   "text": "If your mind wanders, by wanders I mean if you start thinking about other things,"
  },
  {
   "start": 351.53,
   "end": 354.33,
   "text": "that's completely fine."
  },
  {
   "start": 354.18,
   "end": 356.27,
   "text": "That's not failure."
  },
  {
   "start": 356.12,
   "end": 359.78,
   "text": "That's just what minds do."
  },
  {
   "start": 359.63,
   "end": 365.58,
   "text": "Gently, without frustration, just notice it happened, and then come back here,"
  },
  {
   "start": 365.43,
   "end": 370.54,
   "text": "to this breath, to this moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 370.39,
   "end": 373.04,
   "text": "Exhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 372.89,
   "end": 383.18,
   "text": "Try this now."
  },
  {
   "start": 383.03,
   "end": 393.48,
   "text": "Bring to mind that same worried thought from earlier, that same small stone you noticed."
  },
  {
   "start": 393.33,
   "end": 397.0,
   "text": "Let yourself touch it once, just briefly."
  },
  {
   "start": 396.85,
   "end": 400.94,
   "text": "And now, gently, put it back down."
  },
  {
   "start": 400.79,
   "end": 402.96,
   "text": "Not by force."
  },
  {
   "start": 402.81,
   "end": 406.06,
   "text": "Not by pushing it away hard."
  },
  {
   "start": 405.91,
   "end": 412.82,
   "text": "Just by turning your attention back here, to your breath, to your body,"
  },
  {
   "start": 412.67,
   "end": 418.55,
   "text": "to this present moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 418.4,
   "end": 419.05,
   "text": "Inhale."
  },
  {
   "start": 418.88,
   "end": 430.18,
   "text": "And notice, right now, the physical feeling of sitting or lying down."
  },
  {
   "start": 430.03,
   "end": 439.24,
   "text": "The weight of your body."
  },
  {
   "start": 439.09,
   "end": 439.74,
   "text": "The temperature of the air around you."
  },
  {
   "start": 439.11,
   "end": 441.76,
   "text": "These things are only happening now."
  },
  {
   "start": 441.61,
   "end": 445.64,
   "text": "They're not thoughts about the past or future."
  },
  {
   "start": 445.49,
   "end": 453.61,
   "text": "They're simply what's real, right in this moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 453.46,
   "end": 463.03,
   "text": "And exhale completely."
  },
  {
   "start": 462.88,
   "end": 467.17,
   "text": "Overthinking will probably visit again later today."
  },
  {
   "start": 467.02,
   "end": 468.33,
   "text": "That's alright."
  },
  {
   "start": 468.18,
   "end": 471.55,
   "text": "It's just something minds do sometimes."
  },
  {
   "start": 471.4,
   "end": 473.87,
   "text": "But you know a way back."
  },
  {
   "start": 473.72,
   "end": 484.61,
   "text": "Right here, to your breath, to your body, to this present moment, whenever you need it."
  },
  {
   "start": 484.46,
   "end": 491.82,
   "text": "And if you\u2019d like, you can repeat a few phrases after me."
  },
  {
   "start": 491.67,
   "end": 498.08,
   "text": "I don't have to solve every thought that visits me."
  },
  {
   "start": 497.93,
   "end": 505.01,
   "text": "I don't have to solve every thought that visits me."
  },
  {
   "start": 504.86,
   "end": 512.93,
   "text": "I can gently return here, to this breath, whenever I need to."
  },
  {
   "start": 512.78,
   "end": 523.6,
   "text": "I can gently return here, to this breath, whenever I need to."
  },
  {
   "start": 523.45,
   "end": 530.12,
   "text": "The present moment is always available to me."
  },
  {
   "start": 529.97,
   "end": 537.8,
   "text": "The present moment is always available to me."
  },
  {
   "start": 537.65,
   "end": 539.72,
   "text": "I am not my thoughts."
  },
  {
   "start": 539.57,
   "end": 543.71,
   "text": "I am the one noticing them."
  },
  {
   "start": 543.56,
   "end": 546.51,
   "text": "I am not my thoughts."
  },
  {
   "start": 546.36,
   "end": 553.19,
   "text": "I am the one noticing them."
  },
  {
   "start": 553.04,
   "end": 557.55,
   "text": "Right now I am safe."
  },
  {
   "start": 557.4,
   "end": 563.59,
   "text": "Right now I am safe."
  },
  {
   "start": 563.44,
   "end": 570.08,
   "text": "Take one more slow inhale."
  },
  {
   "start": 569.93,
   "end": 580.76,
   "text": "And exhale, completely."
  },
  {
   "start": 580.61,
   "end": 587.7,
   "text": "When you're ready to come back, start noticing small things around you."
  },
  {
   "start": 587.55,
   "end": 592.02,
   "text": "Whatever is supporting your body right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 591.87,
   "end": 594.0,
   "text": "Sounds nearby."
  },
  {
   "start": 593.85,
   "end": 594.92,
   "text": "Your breath."
  },
  {
   "start": 594.77,
   "end": 599.23,
   "text": "Move your fingers gently."
  },
  {
   "start": 599.08,
   "end": 601.91,
   "text": "Then move your feet."
  },
  {
   "start": 601.76,
   "end": 609.0,
   "text": "Whenever it feels right, let your eyes open."
  }
 ]
}

assets/content/episodes/c005/cues.json:
{
 "source": "faster-whisper small.en word timestamps aligned to script phrases",
 "matchedWords": 936,
 "scriptWords": 962,
 "cues": [
  {
   "start": 0.22,
   "end": 5.02,
   "text": "Hello, lovely English learner."
  },
  {
   "start": 4.87,
   "end": 9.81,
   "text": "Take a moment to settle in."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.66,
   "end": 15.15,
   "text": "It doesn\u2019t matter where you are or what kind of day you\u2019ve had."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.0,
   "end": 21.59,
   "text": "Right now, you can just be here."
  },
  {
   "start": 21.44,
   "end": 24.52,
   "text": "Find a comfortable position."
  },
  {
   "start": 24.37,
   "end": 30.06,
   "text": "You can sit down or lie down, whatever feels good for you today."
  },
  {
   "start": 29.91,
   "end": 39.29,
   "text": "And just give yourself permission to slow down a little."
  },
  {
   "start": 39.14,
   "end": 47.03,
   "text": "I\u2019m here with you, and for the next few minutes, I\u2019ll help you quiet your mind and relax,"
  },
  {
   "start": 46.88,
   "end": 50.98,
   "text": "okay?"
  },
  {
   "start": 50.83,
   "end": 53.0,
   "text": "You can gently close your eyes."
  },
  {
   "start": 52.85,
   "end": 56.48,
   "text": "Or, if you\u2019d rather keep them open,"
  },
  {
   "start": 56.33,
   "end": 64.41,
   "text": "just let your eyes rest softly on something in front of you."
  },
  {
   "start": 64.26,
   "end": 69.51,
   "text": "There\u2019s nowhere else you need to be right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 69.36,
   "end": 76.1,
   "text": "Just stay here with me for a moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 75.95,
   "end": 79.6,
   "text": "Notice what\u2019s under your body."
  },
  {
   "start": 79.45,
   "end": 84.16,
   "text": "Maybe it\u2019s a chair, a bed, or the floor."
  },
  {
   "start": 84.01,
   "end": 88.25,
   "text": "Feel it supporting you."
  },
  {
   "start": 88.1,
   "end": 92.27,
   "text": "Let your shoulders relax."
  },
  {
   "start": 92.12,
   "end": 96.58,
   "text": "Let your hands rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 96.43,
   "end": 105.39,
   "text": "And now, take a slow breath in\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 105.24,
   "end": 111.92,
   "text": "Today, we're going to explore two very different states."
  },
  {
   "start": 111.77,
   "end": 116.84,
   "text": "Your mind and body move between these two states constantly,"
  },
  {
   "start": 116.69,
   "end": 120.78,
   "text": "sometimes without you even noticing."
  },
  {
   "start": 120.63,
   "end": 126.48,
   "text": "The first state is to be active."
  },
  {
   "start": 126.33,
   "end": 134.79,
   "text": "To be active means to be busy doing things, moving, or thinking about many things."
  },
  {
   "start": 134.64,
   "end": 140.95,
   "text": "The second state is to rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 140.8,
   "end": 147.26,
   "text": "To rest means to stop what you\u2019re doing for a while, relax,"
  },
  {
   "start": 147.11,
   "end": 153.94,
   "text": "and let your body and mind become calm."
  },
  {
   "start": 153.79,
   "end": 158.32,
   "text": "Right now, notice your mind."
  },
  {
   "start": 158.17,
   "end": 160.15,
   "text": "Is it busy?"
  },
  {
   "start": 160.0,
   "end": 164.02,
   "text": "Is it active, moving from thought to thought?"
  },
  {
   "start": 163.87,
   "end": 166.44,
   "text": "That's completely normal."
  },
  {
   "start": 166.29,
   "end": 172.78,
   "text": "Minds are often active, especially after a long day."
  },
  {
   "start": 172.63,
   "end": 181.96,
   "text": "Let's gently guide your mind from being active, toward resting."
  },
  {
   "start": 181.81,
   "end": 185.2,
   "text": "Start with your breath."
  },
  {
   "start": 185.05,
   "end": 192.97,
   "text": "Notice it moving in, and moving out."
  },
  {
   "start": 192.82,
   "end": 199.31,
   "text": "This simple noticing already begins to slow things down."
  },
  {
   "start": 199.16,
   "end": 201.73,
   "text": "Breathing in slowly\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 201.58,
   "end": 209.88,
   "text": "and breathing out slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 209.73,
   "end": 216.88,
   "text": "Notice how your breath, all by itself, doesn't need to be active."
  },
  {
   "start": 216.73,
   "end": 226.08,
   "text": "It simply flows, gently, at its own steady pace."
  },
  {
   "start": 225.93,
   "end": 231.25,
   "text": "Let your body flow this same rhythm."
  },
  {
   "start": 231.1,
   "end": 234.32,
   "text": "Let your shoulders rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 234.17,
   "end": 238.42,
   "text": "Let your hands rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 238.27,
   "end": 246.92,
   "text": "Let your legs feel heavy, and still."
  },
  {
   "start": 246.77,
   "end": 253.5,
   "text": "If your mind feels active right now, with a lot of thoughts, that\u2019s okay."
  },
  {
   "start": 253.35,
   "end": 255.64,
   "text": "You don\u2019t need to stop your thoughts."
  },
  {
   "start": 255.49,
   "end": 259.36,
   "text": "Just notice them."
  },
  {
   "start": 259.21,
   "end": 267.25,
   "text": "And slowly, without trying too hard, let your body rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 267.1,
   "end": 274.84,
   "text": "Your mind can take a little more time to become calm."
  },
  {
   "start": 274.69,
   "end": 277.31,
   "text": "Take another breath in\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 277.16,
   "end": 283.86,
   "text": "and out."
  },
  {
   "start": 283.71,
   "end": 289.48,
   "text": "Imagine, for a moment, that your mind is like a busy street, full of movement,"
  },
  {
   "start": 289.33,
   "end": 290.76,
   "text": "full of sound."
  },
  {
   "start": 290.61,
   "end": 298.74,
   "text": "And your breath is like a quiet room nearby, where you can step in, and rest,"
  },
  {
   "start": 298.59,
   "end": 304.02,
   "text": "whenever you choose."
  },
  {
   "start": 303.87,
   "end": 312.61,
   "text": "Right now, step gently into that quiet room."
  },
  {
   "start": 312.46,
   "end": 321.79,
   "text": "Notice how it feels here, calmer, softer, slower."
  },
  {
   "start": 321.64,
   "end": 325.98,
   "text": "You don't need to close the busy street outside."
  },
  {
   "start": 325.83,
   "end": 331.54,
   "text": "It can stay there, active, as it always is."
  },
  {
   "start": 331.39,
   "end": 340.34,
   "text": "You're simply choosing, for this moment, to rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 340.19,
   "end": 344.17,
   "text": "Bring your attention to your body."
  },
  {
   "start": 344.02,
   "end": 349.63,
   "text": "Notice any place that still feels active, tense, or alert."
  },
  {
   "start": 349.48,
   "end": 351.69,
   "text": "Maybe your shoulders."
  },
  {
   "start": 351.54,
   "end": 353.31,
   "text": "Maybe your face."
  },
  {
   "start": 353.16,
   "end": 355.96,
   "text": "Maybe your hands."
  },
  {
   "start": 355.81,
   "end": 361.99,
   "text": "Gently invite that part to rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 361.84,
   "end": 370.93,
   "text": "Not by force, but by simply allowing it."
  },
  {
   "start": 370.78,
   "end": 374.71,
   "text": "Let it soften, just a little more."
  },
  {
   "start": 374.56,
   "end": 379.83,
   "text": "Take a breath in\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 379.68,
   "end": 386.28,
   "text": "and out."
  },
  {
   "start": 386.13,
   "end": 395.25,
   "text": "Notice how your body can rest, even if your mind still holds a few active thoughts."
  },
  {
   "start": 395.1,
   "end": 398.98,
   "text": "The two don't need to match perfectly."
  },
  {
   "start": 398.83,
   "end": 407.7,
   "text": "Your body can lead the way, showing your mind how to slow down."
  },
  {
   "start": 407.55,
   "end": 410.86,
   "text": "Let's continue."
  },
  {
   "start": 410.71,
   "end": 417.76,
   "text": "Bring your awareness to your chest, rising and falling gently with each breath."
  },
  {
   "start": 417.61,
   "end": 425.64,
   "text": "Notice how naturally this movement happens, without effort,"
  },
  {
   "start": 425.49,
   "end": 431.26,
   "text": "without needing to be active at all."
  },
  {
   "start": 431.11,
   "end": 438.56,
   "text": "Let your whole body settle a little more."
  },
  {
   "start": 438.41,
   "end": 444.7,
   "text": "If a thought arrives, active and quick, simply notice it,"
  },
  {
   "start": 444.55,
   "end": 449.28,
   "text": "the way you might notice a bird flying past a window."
  },
  {
   "start": 449.13,
   "end": 451.22,
   "text": "You don't need to follow it."
  },
  {
   "start": 451.07,
   "end": 460.22,
   "text": "You can simply let it pass, and return to resting."
  },
  {
   "start": 460.07,
   "end": 463.41,
   "text": "Take another slow breath in\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 463.26,
   "end": 469.83,
   "text": "and out."
  },
  {
   "start": 469.68,
   "end": 482.1,
   "text": "There\u2019s something important to remember: Resting doesn\u2019t mean that nothing is happening."
  },
  {
   "start": 481.95,
   "end": 485.48,
   "text": "Your heart is still beating."
  },
  {
   "start": 485.33,
   "end": 487.65,
   "text": "You\u2019re still breathing."
  },
  {
   "start": 487.5,
   "end": 495.22,
   "text": "Your body is still working quietly, even while you rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 495.07,
   "end": 506.96,
   "text": "Rest simply means slowing down and allowing your body and mind to be calm for a while."
  },
  {
   "start": 506.81,
   "end": 514.83,
   "text": "Let your body stay here and rest for a little longer."
  },
  {
   "start": 514.68,
   "end": 518.42,
   "text": "You don\u2019t need to be active right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 518.27,
   "end": 521.49,
   "text": "You don\u2019t need to hurry."
  },
  {
   "start": 521.34,
   "end": 528.96,
   "text": "Just enjoy this quiet moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 528.81,
   "end": 535.23,
   "text": "And let these gentle words stay with you."
  },
  {
   "start": 535.08,
   "end": 545.33,
   "text": "If you like, you can repeat them out loud or just say them quietly in your mind."
  },
  {
   "start": 545.18,
   "end": 549.43,
   "text": "Here we go:"
  },
  {
   "start": 549.28,
   "end": 557.84,
   "text": "I can rest, even when my mind feels busy."
  },
  {
   "start": 557.69,
   "end": 566.22,
   "text": "My body knows how to slow down."
  },
  {
   "start": 566.07,
   "end": 574.82,
   "text": "I don't need to control every thought."
  },
  {
   "start": 574.67,
   "end": 579.39,
   "text": "I am calm."
  },
  {
   "start": 579.24,
   "end": 587.91,
   "text": "I am safe, resting here."
  },
  {
   "start": 587.76,
   "end": 596.0,
   "text": "Take another slow breath, and let these words settle a little deeper."
  },
  {
   "start": 595.85,
   "end": 602.28,
   "text": "Stay here for a while longer, simply resting."
  },
  {
   "start": 602.13,
   "end": 607.25,
   "text": "If your mind becomes active again, that's completely fine."
  },
  {
   "start": 607.1,
   "end": 619.18,
   "text": "Just notice, gently, and return to resting, as many times as you need."
  },
  {
   "start": 619.03,
   "end": 627.95,
   "text": "This movement between active and rest happens constantly, all day, every day."
  },
  {
   "start": 627.8,
   "end": 630.28,
   "text": "There's no need to fight it."
  },
  {
   "start": 630.13,
   "end": 644.59,
   "text": "You're simply learning to notice it, and to choose rest, whenever you have the chance."
  },
  {
   "start": 644.44,
   "end": 652.56,
   "text": "When you feel ready, slowly notice the room around you again."
  },
  {
   "start": 652.41,
   "end": 659.86,
   "text": "Notice what\u2019s under your body, maybe a chair, a bed, or the floor."
  },
  {
   "start": 659.71,
   "end": 662.02,
   "text": "Notice your breathing."
  },
  {
   "start": 661.87,
   "end": 669.52,
   "text": "It\u2019s still slow and calm."
  },
  {
   "start": 669.37,
   "end": 674.52,
   "text": "Let your fingers move first, just slightly."
  },
  {
   "start": 674.37,
   "end": 676.78,
   "text": "Then your toes."
  },
  {
   "start": 676.63,
   "end": 683.99,
   "text": "Small movements, gentle and unhurried."
  },
  {
   "start": 683.84,
   "end": 688.24,
   "text": "Take your time."
  },
  {
   "start": 688.09,
   "end": 692.12,
   "text": "There's no need to rush back into being active."
  },
  {
   "start": 691.97,
   "end": 709.5,
   "text": "Whenever you're ready, let your eyes open softly, taking in the light around you."
  },
  {
   "start": 709.35,
   "end": 715.56,
   "text": "Carry this rest with you, into whatever comes next."
  },
  {
   "start": 715.41,
   "end": 726.65,
   "text": "And remember, even in the middle of a busy, active day, you can always return here,"
  },
  {
   "start": 726.5,
   "end": 737.49,
   "text": "to this quiet stillness, whenever you need it."
  },
  {
   "start": 737.34,
   "end": 740.36,
   "text": "You are calm."
  },
  {
   "start": 740.21,
   "end": 743.86,
   "text": "You are rested."
  },
  {
   "start": 743.71,
   "end": 783.0,
   "text": "And you are exactly where you need to be."
  }
 ]
}

assets/content/episodes/c007/cues.json:
{
 "source": "faster-whisper small.en word timestamps aligned to script phrases",
 "matchedWords": 848,
 "scriptWords": 859,
 "cues": [
  {
   "start": 0.91,
   "end": 3.2,
   "text": "Hi there!"
  },
  {
   "start": 3.05,
   "end": 10.24,
   "text": "Today's meditation is \u201cFinding a Little Inner Calm\u201d."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.09,
   "end": 14.64,
   "text": "Take a moment to get comfortable."
  },
  {
   "start": 14.49,
   "end": 19.66,
   "text": "You might have had a busy day, a long morning,"
  },
  {
   "start": 19.51,
   "end": 25.32,
   "text": "or maybe you\u2019re just looking for a little time to yourself."
  },
  {
   "start": 25.17,
   "end": 31.74,
   "text": "Whatever brought you here, you don\u2019t need to change anything right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.59,
   "end": 37.6,
   "text": "Just let yourself settle."
  },
  {
   "start": 37.45,
   "end": 46.28,
   "text": "You can close your eyes if that feels comfortable, or keep them open if you prefer."
  },
  {
   "start": 46.13,
   "end": 51.78,
   "text": "For the next few minutes, there\u2019s nowhere else you need to be."
  },
  {
   "start": 51.63,
   "end": 68.14,
   "text": "Just take a breath, slow things down, and be here for a while."
  },
  {
   "start": 67.99,
   "end": 70.76,
   "text": "Let's begin."
  },
  {
   "start": 70.61,
   "end": 73.96,
   "text": "I want you to check in for a moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 73.81,
   "end": 78.44,
   "text": "Notice your body, right now, exactly as it is."
  },
  {
   "start": 78.29,
   "end": 83.29,
   "text": "Not judging it, just noticing."
  },
  {
   "start": 83.14,
   "end": 88.04,
   "text": "Is there a little tension anywhere?"
  },
  {
   "start": 87.89,
   "end": 93.54,
   "text": "A slight tightness in your jaw, maybe?"
  },
  {
   "start": 93.39,
   "end": 103.68,
   "text": "A mind that keeps jumping from one thing to the next, unable to fully land on anything."
  },
  {
   "start": 103.53,
   "end": 112.2,
   "text": "If you're noticing any of that, that's what we'd call feeling restless."
  },
  {
   "start": 112.05,
   "end": 120.52,
   "text": "Restless means your body or mind can't quite calm down, it keeps moving,"
  },
  {
   "start": 120.37,
   "end": 127.1,
   "text": "searching for something, even when there's nowhere it actually needs to go."
  },
  {
   "start": 126.95,
   "end": 135.66,
   "text": "Think of it like a bird that keeps hopping from branch to branch,"
  },
  {
   "start": 135.51,
   "end": 140.94,
   "text": "never quite landing anywhere long enough to rest."
  },
  {
   "start": 140.79,
   "end": 151.42,
   "text": "Notice, gently, if there is a little restlessness in you right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 151.27,
   "end": 157.88,
   "text": "Restlessness is the noun, the feeling itself."
  },
  {
   "start": 157.73,
   "end": 165.42,
   "text": "Restless is the adjective, it describes how you feel."
  },
  {
   "start": 165.27,
   "end": 170.8,
   "text": "You don\u2019t need to fix it or make it go away."
  },
  {
   "start": 170.65,
   "end": 176.96,
   "text": "Just notice it\u2019s there."
  },
  {
   "start": 176.81,
   "end": 187.52,
   "text": "Inhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 187.37,
   "end": 190.32,
   "text": "Restlessness isn't wrong, by the way."
  },
  {
   "start": 190.17,
   "end": 192.62,
   "text": "It's just energy."
  },
  {
   "start": 192.47,
   "end": 199.98,
   "text": "Most of us carry a little of it, most days, especially after a long day, or a busy one."
  },
  {
   "start": 199.83,
   "end": 204.6,
   "text": "A busy day at work, for example."
  },
  {
   "start": 204.45,
   "end": 215.46,
   "text": "Exhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 215.31,
   "end": 221.76,
   "text": "Let\u2019s give that energy a moment to slow down."
  },
  {
   "start": 221.61,
   "end": 228.52,
   "text": "Bring your attention to your feet, wherever they are right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 228.37,
   "end": 236.36,
   "text": "Notice them, simply resting, touching the floor, or the bed."
  },
  {
   "start": 236.21,
   "end": 238.64,
   "text": "They're not going anywhere."
  },
  {
   "start": 238.49,
   "end": 242.76,
   "text": "They don't need to move."
  },
  {
   "start": 242.61,
   "end": 256.22,
   "text": "Breathe in slowly, and imagine your feet becoming a little heavier."
  },
  {
   "start": 256.07,
   "end": 262.96,
   "text": "Breathe out, and let that feeling move gently into your legs."
  },
  {
   "start": 262.81,
   "end": 273.14,
   "text": "Let your legs become a little heavier."
  },
  {
   "start": 272.99,
   "end": 280.34,
   "text": "Notice how this feels different from the busy feeling you felt before."
  },
  {
   "start": 280.19,
   "end": 284.0,
   "text": "You don\u2019t need to think about what comes next."
  },
  {
   "start": 283.85,
   "end": 295.24,
   "text": "Just notice your body here, feeling calm, heavy, and still."
  },
  {
   "start": 295.09,
   "end": 302.86,
   "text": "Inhale again."
  },
  {
   "start": 302.71,
   "end": 312.56,
   "text": "Yeah, so this feeling has a name too, and the name is settled."
  },
  {
   "start": 312.41,
   "end": 317.4,
   "text": "Settled means your body and mind have finally stopped searching,"
  },
  {
   "start": 317.25,
   "end": 323.5,
   "text": "and simply rested into where they already are."
  },
  {
   "start": 323.35,
   "end": 330.26,
   "text": "Think of it like the same bird from earlier, finally choosing one branch,"
  },
  {
   "start": 330.11,
   "end": 338.32,
   "text": "and staying there, quiet, and still, relaxed."
  },
  {
   "start": 338.17,
   "end": 347.4,
   "text": "Exhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 347.25,
   "end": 352.0,
   "text": "Let this settled feeling continue spreading."
  },
  {
   "start": 351.85,
   "end": 360.0,
   "text": "Spreading from your legs, up into your stomach, your chest."
  },
  {
   "start": 359.85,
   "end": 372.08,
   "text": "Notice your breath, still moving, but slower now, calmer, with nowhere urgent to be."
  },
  {
   "start": 371.93,
   "end": 380.22,
   "text": "Inhale, feeling this quiet weight rest in your chest."
  },
  {
   "start": 380.07,
   "end": 386.14,
   "text": "Exhale, releasing anything that still feels restless,"
  },
  {
   "start": 385.99,
   "end": 395.14,
   "text": "anything still searching for something else."
  },
  {
   "start": 394.99,
   "end": 399.64,
   "text": "Notice your shoulders now."
  },
  {
   "start": 399.49,
   "end": 405.44,
   "text": "Let them drop a little further, settling completely,"
  },
  {
   "start": 405.29,
   "end": 414.32,
   "text": "the way that bird's wings finally fold, once it's found its branch."
  },
  {
   "start": 414.17,
   "end": 422.64,
   "text": "Inhale slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 422.49,
   "end": 428.18,
   "text": "And your hands, wherever they're resting right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 428.03,
   "end": 432.32,
   "text": "Let them be heavy, and still."
  },
  {
   "start": 432.17,
   "end": 439.0,
   "text": "Nothing left to hold onto, nothing left to search for."
  },
  {
   "start": 438.85,
   "end": 448.32,
   "text": "Exhale completely."
  },
  {
   "start": 448.17,
   "end": 453.94,
   "text": "Notice how your mind feels right now, too."
  },
  {
   "start": 453.79,
   "end": 459.56,
   "text": "It might still be a little busy, and that\u2019s okay."
  },
  {
   "start": 459.41,
   "end": 465.66,
   "text": "Maybe it feels a little quieter than before, even if only a little."
  },
  {
   "start": 465.51,
   "end": 469.38,
   "text": "That\u2019s also okay."
  },
  {
   "start": 469.23,
   "end": 473.78,
   "text": "You don\u2019t need to force yourself to feel calm."
  },
  {
   "start": 473.63,
   "end": 478.42,
   "text": "You are not trying to stop feeling restless forever."
  },
  {
   "start": 478.27,
   "end": 486.54,
   "text": "You\u2019re simply practicing landing here, in this present moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 486.39,
   "end": 496.42,
   "text": "When we say \u201clanding,\u201d we mean arriving and becoming settled in a place or moment."
  },
  {
   "start": 496.27,
   "end": 500.64,
   "text": "We use this word for planes when they arrive on the ground,"
  },
  {
   "start": 500.49,
   "end": 507.64,
   "text": "but we can also use it when we talk about meditation."
  },
  {
   "start": 507.49,
   "end": 516.14,
   "text": "For these few minutes, you\u2019re simply giving yourself time to arrive here, to land here,"
  },
  {
   "start": 515.99,
   "end": 521.26,
   "text": "and be still."
  },
  {
   "start": 521.11,
   "end": 526.12,
   "text": "Inhale."
  },
  {
   "start": 525.97,
   "end": 541.68,
   "text": "And exhale, long, and slow."
  },
  {
   "start": 541.53,
   "end": 547.46,
   "text": "Now, a few words, if you'd like to hold onto them."
  },
  {
   "start": 547.31,
   "end": 552.88,
   "text": "I don't need to search for anything right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 552.73,
   "end": 559.8,
   "text": "I don't need to search for anything right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 559.65,
   "end": 567.44,
   "text": "I am allowed to settle, exactly where I am."
  },
  {
   "start": 567.29,
   "end": 575.44,
   "text": "I am allowed to settle, exactly where I am."
  },
  {
   "start": 575.29,
   "end": 581.46,
   "text": "Restlessness can visit, and it can also leave."
  },
  {
   "start": 581.31,
   "end": 589.0,
   "text": "Restlessness can visit, and it can also leave."
  },
  {
   "start": 588.85,
   "end": 595.62,
   "text": "My body knows how to rest, even when my mind is busy."
  },
  {
   "start": 595.47,
   "end": 604.84,
   "text": "My body knows how to rest, even when my mind is busy."
  },
  {
   "start": 604.69,
   "end": 610.82,
   "text": "I am settling, a little more, with every breath."
  },
  {
   "start": 610.67,
   "end": 618.9,
   "text": "I am settling, a little more, with every breath."
  },
  {
   "start": 618.75,
   "end": 622.16,
   "text": "Take one more slow breath in."
  },
  {
   "start": 622.01,
   "end": 634.12,
   "text": "And breathe out, completely."
  },
  {
   "start": 633.97,
   "end": 638.9,
   "text": "You can stay here for a little longer if you\u2019d like."
  },
  {
   "start": 638.75,
   "end": 643.78,
   "text": "You can take a few moments to notice how your body feels."
  },
  {
   "start": 643.63,
   "end": 649.98,
   "text": "And when you\u2019re ready to come back, start noticing what is around you."
  },
  {
   "start": 649.83,
   "end": 657.28,
   "text": "Feel the chair, floor, or bed supporting your body."
  },
  {
   "start": 657.13,
   "end": 662.08,
   "text": "Notice any sounds you can hear."
  },
  {
   "start": 661.93,
   "end": 669.46,
   "text": "Then notice your breathing, slow and easy."
  },
  {
   "start": 669.31,
   "end": 673.6,
   "text": "Gently move your fingers."
  },
  {
   "start": 673.45,
   "end": 678.98,
   "text": "Then move your feet."
  },
  {
   "start": 678.83,
   "end": 687.0,
   "text": "And whenever you\u2019re ready, slowly open your eyes."
  }
 ]
}

assets/content/episodes/c008/cues.json:
{
 "source": "faster-whisper small.en word timestamps aligned to script phrases",
 "matchedWords": 725,
 "scriptWords": 804,
 "cues": [
  {
   "start": 0.35,
   "end": 4.12,
   "text": "Good to have you here."
  },
  {
   "start": 3.97,
   "end": 9.22,
   "text": "However you're sitting right now, let that be enough."
  },
  {
   "start": 9.07,
   "end": 10.66,
   "text": "No adjusting, no fixing."
  },
  {
   "start": 10.51,
   "end": 15.76,
   "text": "Just arrive, exactly as you are."
  },
  {
   "start": 15.61,
   "end": 20.69,
   "text": "You can be quiet to yourself."
  },
  {
   "start": 20.54,
   "end": 28.95,
   "text": "Let your eyes close, or let them go soft, resting downward."
  },
  {
   "start": 28.8,
   "end": 30.73,
   "text": "Nothing to prepare for."
  },
  {
   "start": 30.58,
   "end": 31.73,
   "text": "Nothing to get right."
  },
  {
   "start": 31.58,
   "end": 37.68,
   "text": "Just you, and a little quiet time."
  },
  {
   "start": 37.53,
   "end": 42.35,
   "text": "Breathe in."
  },
  {
   "start": 42.2,
   "end": 47.46,
   "text": "Let it out slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 47.31,
   "end": 49.3,
   "text": "One more."
  },
  {
   "start": 49.15,
   "end": 50.46,
   "text": "In\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 50.31,
   "end": 57.8,
   "text": "and out."
  },
  {
   "start": 57.65,
   "end": 61.28,
   "text": "I want to tell you something you probably already know,"
  },
  {
   "start": 61.13,
   "end": 65.88,
   "text": "but maybe haven't thought about in a while."
  },
  {
   "start": 65.73,
   "end": 70.36,
   "text": "Everyone has a voice inside them."
  },
  {
   "start": 70.21,
   "end": 81.9,
   "text": "A voice that talks to you, quietly, all day long, especially when something goes wrong."
  },
  {
   "start": 81.75,
   "end": 87.0,
   "text": "Let's think about that voice for a minute."
  },
  {
   "start": 86.85,
   "end": 94.04,
   "text": "Imagine, just for a second, you did something small today."
  },
  {
   "start": 93.89,
   "end": 96.14,
   "text": "Nothing serious."
  },
  {
   "start": 95.99,
   "end": 98.04,
   "text": "Maybe you forgot something."
  },
  {
   "start": 97.89,
   "end": 101.0,
   "text": "Maybe you said the wrong thing to someone."
  },
  {
   "start": 100.85,
   "end": 106.28,
   "text": "Maybe you made a little mistake at work, or at home."
  },
  {
   "start": 106.13,
   "end": 115.46,
   "text": "Now notice, in your mind, how that inner voice usually reacts to something like that."
  },
  {
   "start": 115.31,
   "end": 119.0,
   "text": "For a lot of people, that voice gets sharp pretty fast."
  },
  {
   "start": 118.85,
   "end": 126.38,
   "text": "That's what we'd call being self-critical."
  },
  {
   "start": 126.23,
   "end": 130.7,
   "text": "Self-critical means talking to yourself harshly,"
  },
  {
   "start": 130.55,
   "end": 135.67,
   "text": "the way you'd never actually talk to someone you cared about."
  },
  {
   "start": 135.52,
   "end": 146.58,
   "text": "It sounds like, \"Why did I do that?\" or \"I always mess things up.\" It's quick to blame."
  },
  {
   "start": 146.43,
   "end": 151.6,
   "text": "Slow to forgive."
  },
  {
   "start": 151.45,
   "end": 155.69,
   "text": "Notice if that voice feels familiar to you."
  },
  {
   "start": 155.54,
   "end": 161.87,
   "text": "No need to judge it, just notice it."
  },
  {
   "start": 161.72,
   "end": 166.26,
   "text": "Breathe in."
  },
  {
   "start": 166.11,
   "end": 170.32,
   "text": "Now, here's something worth imagining."
  },
  {
   "start": 170.17,
   "end": 173.72,
   "text": "Picture a close friend of yours."
  },
  {
   "start": 173.57,
   "end": 176.37,
   "text": "Someone you actually love."
  },
  {
   "start": 176.22,
   "end": 179.49,
   "text": "Now imagine that same friend comes to you,"
  },
  {
   "start": 179.34,
   "end": 186.6,
   "text": "and tells you they made that exact same mistake you made earlier today."
  },
  {
   "start": 186.45,
   "end": 190.59,
   "text": "What would you actually say to them?"
  },
  {
   "start": 190.44,
   "end": 191.09,
   "text": "Chances are,"
  },
  {
   "start": 190.9,
   "end": 197.26,
   "text": "you wouldn't say \"you always mess things up.\" You'd probably say something softer."
  },
  {
   "start": 197.11,
   "end": 206.02,
   "text": "Something like, \"It's okay, it happens.\" Or \"You're being too hard on yourself."
  },
  {
   "start": 205.87,
   "end": 210.9,
   "text": "It\u2019s okay to make mistakes.\""
  },
  {
   "start": 210.75,
   "end": 211.9,
   "text": "That kind,"
  },
  {
   "start": 211.75,
   "end": 224.08,
   "text": "gentle voice\u2014the one you naturally use with people you love\u2014that\u2019s called being self-compassionate."
  },
  {
   "start": 223.93,
   "end": 226.51,
   "text": "Self-compassionate, such a beautiful word."
  },
  {
   "start": 226.36,
   "end": 234.71,
   "text": "Being self-compassionate means treating yourself with the same kindness you\u2019d give to a friend:"
  },
  {
   "start": 234.56,
   "end": 244.49,
   "text": "warmth instead of judgment, understanding instead of blame."
  },
  {
   "start": 244.34,
   "end": 253.37,
   "text": "Repeat with me: \u201cI can be self-compassionate.\u201d"
  },
  {
   "start": 253.22,
   "end": 260.4,
   "text": "Breathe out slowly."
  },
  {
   "start": 260.25,
   "end": 262.02,
   "text": "Here's the interesting part."
  },
  {
   "start": 261.87,
   "end": 265.64,
   "text": "You already know how to be self-compassionate."
  },
  {
   "start": 265.49,
   "end": 269.31,
   "text": "You do it all the time, for other people."
  },
  {
   "start": 269.16,
   "end": 271.31,
   "text": "The voice isn't missing."
  },
  {
   "start": 271.16,
   "end": 277.8,
   "text": "It's just usually pointed somewhere else, away from yourself."
  },
  {
   "start": 277.65,
   "end": 286.94,
   "text": "Let's practice pointing it inward, just for these few minutes."
  },
  {
   "start": 286.79,
   "end": 290.58,
   "text": "Think again about that small mistake from earlier."
  },
  {
   "start": 290.43,
   "end": 292.4,
   "text": "Or if nothing comes to mind,"
  },
  {
   "start": 292.25,
   "end": 299.71,
   "text": "think of any small thing about yourself you sometimes judge a little too harshly."
  },
  {
   "start": 299.56,
   "end": 303.51,
   "text": "Now, instead of reacting the old way,"
  },
  {
   "start": 303.36,
   "end": 309.38,
   "text": "try speaking to yourself the way you'd speak to that friend."
  },
  {
   "start": 309.23,
   "end": 318.13,
   "text": "Silently, in your mind, try saying something like, \"It's okay."
  },
  {
   "start": 317.98,
   "end": 329.14,
   "text": "You're allowed to make mistakes.\" Or simply, \"You're doing your best.\""
  },
  {
   "start": 328.99,
   "end": 334.9,
   "text": "Notice how that feels, even if it feels a little unfamiliar,"
  },
  {
   "start": 334.75,
   "end": 338.06,
   "text": "even a little strange at first."
  },
  {
   "start": 337.91,
   "end": 341.5,
   "text": "That's completely normal."
  },
  {
   "start": 341.35,
   "end": 346.43,
   "text": "Kindness toward yourself can feel awkward if you're not used to it,"
  },
  {
   "start": 346.28,
   "end": 351.9,
   "text": "like a muscle that hasn't been used in a while."
  },
  {
   "start": 351.75,
   "end": 356.26,
   "text": "Breathe in."
  },
  {
   "start": 356.11,
   "end": 361.05,
   "text": "You don't need to believe these words perfectly, right away."
  },
  {
   "start": 360.9,
   "end": 364.77,
   "text": "You're just practicing."
  },
  {
   "start": 364.62,
   "end": 375.44,
   "text": "Just letting your inner voice soften, a little, right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 375.29,
   "end": 381.84,
   "text": "Self-critical thoughts often show up automatically, fast, and loud."
  },
  {
   "start": 381.69,
   "end": 388.28,
   "text": "Self-compassionate thoughts usually need a little more effort, at least at first."
  },
  {
   "start": 388.13,
   "end": 390.74,
   "text": "They're quieter."
  },
  {
   "start": 390.59,
   "end": 393.31,
   "text": "Gentler."
  },
  {
   "start": 393.16,
   "end": 399.17,
   "text": "They take a moment to choose."
  },
  {
   "start": 399.02,
   "end": 429.33,
   "text": "But every time you choose them, they get a little easier to find."
  },
  {
   "start": 429.18,
   "end": 432.34,
   "text": "Breathe out."
  },
  {
   "start": 432.19,
   "end": 432.84,
   "text": "Imagine, for a moment, that you\u2019re holding your own hand,"
  },
  {
   "start": 432.5,
   "end": 433.15,
   "text": "like you would hold the hand of someone you want to comfort."
  },
  {
   "start": 432.53,
   "end": 433.18,
   "text": "You don't actually need to hold your hand."
  },
  {
   "start": 432.53,
   "end": 433.18,
   "text": "Just imagine the warmth and comfort of that feeling."
  },
  {
   "start": 432.53,
   "end": 433.18,
   "text": "Let yourself receive a little of your own kindness right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 432.53,
   "end": 444.31,
   "text": "A few words, if you'd like to keep them."
  },
  {
   "start": 444.16,
   "end": 450.41,
   "text": "I don't have to be perfect to be worthy of kindness."
  },
  {
   "start": 450.26,
   "end": 458.73,
   "text": "I can talk to myself the way I'd talk to someone I love."
  },
  {
   "start": 458.58,
   "end": 467.59,
   "text": "Mistakes don't make me any less deserving of care."
  },
  {
   "start": 467.44,
   "end": 473.87,
   "text": "I am allowed to be gentle with myself."
  },
  {
   "start": 473.72,
   "end": 478.46,
   "text": "I am doing my best, and that is enough."
  },
  {
   "start": 478.31,
   "end": 487.11,
   "text": "Take one more slow breath in."
  },
  {
   "start": 486.96,
   "end": 491.22,
   "text": "Stay with this feeling a little longer if you'd like."
  },
  {
   "start": 491.07,
   "end": 499.01,
   "text": "There's no rush to leave this softness behind."
  },
  {
   "start": 498.86,
   "end": 506.64,
   "text": "When you're ready to come back, start noticing small, real things again."
  },
  {
   "start": 506.49,
   "end": 510.18,
   "text": "Whatever is supporting your body right now."
  },
  {
   "start": 510.03,
   "end": 512.56,
   "text": "Any sound nearby."
  },
  {
   "start": 512.41,
   "end": 520.51,
   "text": "Your breath, still slow, still yours."
  },
  {
   "start": 520.36,
   "end": 525.73,
   "text": "Move your fingers first, gently."
  },
  {
   "start": 525.58,
   "end": 529.12,
   "text": "Then your feet."
  },
  {
   "start": 528.97,
   "end": 536.74,
   "text": "Whenever it feels right, let your eyes open."
  },
  {
   "start": 536.59,
   "end": 548.92,
   "text": "That kind voice inside you, the one you just practiced listening to, it's always there."
  },
  {
   "start": 548.77,
   "end": 552.4,
   "text": "It doesn't disappear when this meditation ends."
  },
  {
   "start": 552.25,
   "end": 595.0,
   "text": "It's simply waiting for you to reach for it, especially on the days you need it the most."
  }
 ]
}

