   "start": 265.75,
   "end": 276.82,
   "text": "Stay here for a moment and notice all these parts of your body together."
  },
  {
   "start": 276.67,
   "end": 281.3,
   "text": "Relax your forehead."
  },
  {
   "start": 281.15,
   "end": 286.04,
   "text": "Relax your temples."
  },
  {
   "start": 285.89,
   "end": 291.24,
   "text": "Let your jaw become soft."
  },
  {
   "start": 291.09,
   "end": 297.16,
   "text": "Let your shoulders drop."
  },
  {
   "start": 297.01,
   "end": 304.02,
   "text": "Take one more slow breath in\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 303.87,
   "end": 310.46,
   "text": "and breathe out."
  },
  {
   "start": 310.31,
   "end": 316.86,
   "text": "Notice how these parts of your body feel now."
  },
  {
   "start": 316.71,
   "end": 321.24,
   "text": "Maybe they feel a little softer."
  },
  {
   "start": 321.09,
   "end": 326.62,
   "text": "Maybe a little lighter."
  },
  {
   "start": 326.47,
   "end": 336.98,
   "text": "Just stay here for a moment and enjoy this feeling."
  },
  {
   "start": 336.83,
   "end": 344.52,
   "text": "You learned more words than usual today, but don\u2019t worry about remembering them all."
  },
  {
   "start": 344.37,
   "end": 353.64,
   "text": "We\u2019ll use these words again in other meditations, especially the most important ones."
  },
  {
   "start": 353.49,
   "end": 360.8,
   "text": "That\u2019s why it\u2019s important to make these meditations a habit."
  },
  {
   "start": 360.65,
   "end": 367.74,
   "text": "The more you practice, the more you\u2019ll hear the same words again."
  },
  {
   "start": 367.59,
   "end": 377.06,
   "text": "Little by little, you\u2019ll start to remember them naturally, without trying too hard."
  },
  {
   "start": 376.91,
   "end": 387.84,
   "text": "For example, \u201cdrop your shoulders.\u201d You\u2019ll hear this phrase many times in our meditations."
  },
  {
   "start": 387.69,
   "end": 396.26,
   "text": "With time, these words and phrases will start to stay in your mind."
  },
  {
   "start": 396.11,
   "end": 400.02,
   "text": "There\u2019s no rush."
  },
  {
   "start": 399.87,
   "end": 407.16,
   "text": "Now, let\u2019s go back to your forehead."
  },
  {
   "start": 407.01,
   "end": 414.28,
   "text": "Place your whole hand on your forehead and repeat:"
  },
  {
   "start": 414.13,
   "end": 421.9,
   "text": "\u201cI can relax my forehead when I need to.\u201d"
  },
  {
   "start": 421.75,
   "end": 426.84,
   "text": "Notice how your body feels now."
  },
  {
   "start": 426.69,
   "end": 436.36,
   "text": "Your forehead, your temples, your jaw, and your shoulders."
  },
  {
   "start": 436.21,
   "end": 441.54,
   "text": "You don\u2019t need to remember every word right away."
  },
  {
   "start": 441.39,
   "end": 449.32,
   "text": "Your body is already starting to connect these words with the places you\u2019ve touched."
  },
  {
   "start": 449.17,
   "end": 454.24,
   "text": "Take one last slow breath in\u2026"
  },
  {
   "start": 454.09,
   "end": 461.36,
   "text": "and breathe out."
  },
  {
   "start": 461.21,
   "end": 469.3,
   "text": "When you\u2019re ready, slowly open your eyes."
  },
  {
   "start": 469.15,
   "end": 476.54,
   "text": "Carry this relaxed feeling with you as you continue your day."
  },
  {
   "start": 476.39,
   "end": 484.64,
   "text": "And remember, there\u2019s no rush."
  },
  {
   "start": 484.49,
   "end": 498.0,
   "text": "One breath, one word, and one meditation at a time."
  }
 ]
